      "description": "The cooldown of the listed weapons reduces when moving.",
      "notes": "- While Tragic Princess (III) is active, the following weapons gain reduced Cooldown when the player is moving, which include:\n Garlic,  Soul Eater and  Dark Frogamorphosis This content requires the Ode to Castlevania DLC to access\n Santa Water,  La Borra and  Hydro Pump Climax This content requires the Ode to Castlevania DLC to access\n Lightning Ring,  Thunder Loop and  Vjaya Sisters This content requires the Ode to Castlevania DLC to access\n Santa Javelin,  Levelin'Eh, and  Seraphic Cry\n Carréllo\n Fulgur This content requires the Ode to Castlevania DLC to access,  Speculo Fulgur This content requires the Ode to Castlevania DLC to access, and  Tenebris Tonitrus This content requires the Ode to Castlevania DLC to access\n Keremet Bubbles This content requires the Ode to Castlevania DLC to access,  Speculo Keremet Bubbles This content requires the Ode to Castlevania DLC to access, and  Keremet Morbus This content requires the Ode to Castlevania DLC to access\n Kick This content requires the Emerald Diorama DLC to access and  Triangle Kick This content requires the Emerald Diorama DLC to access\n- This cooldown reduction modifier acts independently of the  Cooldown stat, allowing it to reduce the cooldown of listed weapons even after the player has reached -90% Cooldown.\n- Since this Arcana encourages the player to move, it pairs up really well with  Shadow Pinion,  Valkyrie Turner,  Vento Sacro,  Fuwalafuwaloo,  Celestial Dusting and  Valmanway even without directly benefiting from it.\n- The faster the player moves, the greater the Cooldown reduction. This is particularly apparent while using the  Lightning Ring and the  Thunder Loop, owing to their sound cues. Increases to  Move Speed, such as with  Wings, pair up very well with this Arcana, and decreases will weaken it."
