      "description": "Armor also affects listed weapons' damage and reflects enemy damage. Character gains bonus damage depending on missing Health. Defeating enemies with retaliatory damage gives +0.5 Max Health.",
      "notes": "- While Divine Bloodline (IX) is active, multiple effects occur:\r\n- The following weapons now deal +5 flat damage per Armor, up to +250 flat damage:\r\n Cross\r\n King Bible\r\n Garlic\r\n Santa Water\r\n Lightning Ring\r\n Song of Mana\r\n Vento Sacro\r\n Victory Sword\r\n Silver Wind This content requires the Legacy of the Moonspell DLC to access\r\n- All weapons gain +0.1 flat damage per missing HP below the character's Max Health, uncapped.\r\n- Enemies that touch the character take 10 flat damage per Armor.\r\n- Killing any enemy with \"retaliatory damage\" gives the character +0.5 Max Health. Retaliatory damage includes the touch damage from this Arcana, as well as the on-character effects of following weapons:\r\n NO FUTURE\r\n Victory Sword\r\n Pako Battiliar and  Mazo Familiar\r\n Crimson Shroud\r\n Night Sword This content requires the Legacy of the Moonspell DLC to access and  Muramasa This content requires the Legacy of the Moonspell DLC to access\r\n Eskizzibur This content requires the Tides of the Foscari DLC to access and  Legionnaire This content requires the Tides of the Foscari DLC to access\r\n Iron Shield This content requires the Ode to Castlevania DLC to access and  Dark Iron Shield This content requires the Ode to Castlevania DLC to access\r\nDamage does not have to be taken to do retaliatory damage.\r\n Embrace of Gaea\r\n Stone Skull This content requires the Ode to Castlevania DLC to access has innate retaliation damage that is not associated with any weapon.\n- This Arcana has a unique interaction with  Legionnaire This content requires the Tides of the Foscari DLC to access. because the constant stream of clones created by the weapon are considered dealing retaliatory damage, this activates the Arcana's ability with every kill from these clone projectiles. Combined with the fact that current health is not restored at the same time, this also translates to a flat damage increase per enemy killed by the clones provided there's nothing healing the character. With Boogaloo of Illusions (XVIII) that can allow the clones to cover the whole screen and the weapon can wipe out bosses with ease.\r\n- Weapons like  Garlic that deal low but fast ticking damage benefit greatly from the flat damage bonuses.\r\n- The increasing  Might from this Arcana is purely visual and increases by +1% for every flat damage the player gains. With a high enough number, the player can approximate how much more flat damage they are dealing with this value.\r\n- Due to the scaling Max Health that Divine Bloodline (IX) provides, it synergizes well with  Hollow Heart and  Metaglio Left, however the benefit provided by these do not affect any Max Health gained after the items have been leveled."
