      "description": "Listed weapon projectiles explode on impact. Light sources explode. Character explodes when damaged.",
      "notes": "- While Heart of Fire (XIX) is active, the projectiles from the following weapons create an explosion on impact, dealing 50% of base damage (weapons that already have an explosive effect will gain +50% explosive damage instead):\n Fire Wand,  Hellfire,  Aura Blast This content requires the Ode to Castlevania DLC to access and  Kardía Phlegeton This content requires the Ode to Castlevania DLC to access\n Valkyrie Turner,  Svarog Statue This content requires the Ode to Castlevania DLC to access and  Darkness Illusion This content requires the Ode to Castlevania DLC to access\n Phiera Der Tuphello and  Red Muscle\n Zhar Ptytsia\n Tri-Bracelet and  Lapiste Tepisto This content requires the Ode to Castlevania DLC to access\n Flames of Misspell and  Ashes of Muspell\n Ammo Appalate,  Horse Cartridge, and  Gunastrophe\n Prismatic Missile This content requires the Tides of the Foscari DLC to access and  Luminaire This content requires the Tides of the Foscari DLC to access\n Long Gun This content requires the Operation Guns DLC to access and  Prototype A This content requires the Operation Guns DLC to access\n Short Gun This content requires the Operation Guns DLC to access and  Prototype B This content requires the Operation Guns DLC to access\n Spread Shot This content requires the Operation Guns DLC to access and  Prototype C This content requires the Operation Guns DLC to access\n Firearm This content requires the Operation Guns DLC to access and  Fire-L3GS This content requires the Operation Guns DLC to access\n Homing Miss This content requires the Operation Guns DLC to access and  Multistage Missiles This content requires the Operation Guns DLC to access\n Vanitas Whip This content requires the Ode to Castlevania DLC to access and  Aurablaster Tip This content requires the Ode to Castlevania DLC to access\n Raging Fire This content requires the Ode to Castlevania DLC to access,  Speculo Raging Fire This content requires the Ode to Castlevania DLC to access, and  Salamender This content requires the Ode to Castlevania DLC to access\n Hand Grenade This content requires the Ode to Castlevania DLC to access and  The RPG This content requires the Ode to Castlevania DLC to access\n Dies Irae This content requires the Ode to Castlevania DLC to access\n Punch This content requires the Emerald Diorama DLC to access,  Pressure Point This content requires the Emerald Diorama DLC to access and  Gilded Hand This content requires the Emerald Diorama DLC to access\n Saber Machine Gun This content requires the Emerald Diorama DLC to access,  Hecaton Machine Gun This content requires the Emerald Diorama DLC to access and  Divergence This content requires the Emerald Diorama DLC to access\n Super Missile This content requires the Emerald Diorama DLC to access,  Hydra Cannon This content requires the Emerald Diorama DLC to access and  Hyperion Bazooka This content requires the Emerald Diorama DLC to access\n Spirit Rings This content requires the Emerald Diorama DLC to access and  Rings of Calamity This content requires the Emerald Diorama DLC to access\n- The damage caused by these explosions is counted as retaliatory damage, allowing  Armor to increase the damage of the explosions by +10% per point, and also allowing the explosions to increase the player's  Max Health when they defeat enemies if  Divine Bloodline (IX) is active.\n- Note that the explosions caused by weapons are not the same as those triggered by receiving damage or destroying a light source, and thus have different sources of base damage.\n- Heart of Fire (XIX) also causes light sources to explode when destroyed and summons a retaliatory explosion when the player is damaged. When retaliating, it creates an explosion around the character and can retaliate every 0.5 seconds.\n- If none of the listed weapons are present, the explosion from destroying light sources and the retaliatory explosion deals the default base damage of 10. These explosions are affected by  Might and  Area\n- The base damage of Heart of Fire (XIX)'s retaliatory explosions will increase by 5 for every listed weapon held, starting from the second weapon.\n- Additionally, the drop weight of  Nduja Fritta Tantos will be multiplied by 4, making them drop considerably more often from light sources and  Hail from the Future (X).\n- Weapons that have low or no piercing, like the Fire Wand or Long Gun, benefit from this Arcana massively, as it allows them to deal area damage and multiplies their crowd damage output.\r\n- Since the explosion happens per enemy contact, weapons with infinite pierce like Hellfire and Valkyrie Turner (and Gunastrophe) become even more powerful as they shred through enemies while also creating an explosion with each hit. The sheer amount of bullets and later pierce from Phiera Der Tuphello can also create a huge amount of explosions.\r\n- Only the base damage of the weapon is used for the calculation of the explosion damage so Valkyrie Turner's charge up does not affect it.\r\n- Light source and retaliatory explosions deal double damage for Phiera Der Tuphello as it starts with a base damage of 5, this bonus will be overridden by other weapons.\r\n- With  Heir of Fate (XIX), explosions will make defeated enemies drop Scorched Souls that grant  Max Health and  Might when collected.\r\n- All explosions are boosted by  Dario Bossi's ability, making this a highly valuable arcana when setting up a build with him."
